# m01-labels: sourced by make-example-zone and m01-run. Reads
# M01_FAULT_LABELS (comma-separated, five labels, default
# alpha,bravo,charlie,delta,echo) and sets, in this fixed order of faults:
#   M01_L_NOTSERVED  delegated to the child, which does not serve the zone
#   M01_L_DEAD       delegated to an address where nothing answers
#   M01_L_GLUE       two servers; the parent's glue for ns2 is stale
#   M01_L_NSSET      the parent's NS set differs from the zone's
#   M01_L_NODELEG    not delegated at all
# For an assessed run, choose labels the participants have not seen.
m01_labels() {
    local raw=${M01_FAULT_LABELS:-alpha,bravo,charlie,delta,echo} l seen=" good "
    local -a L
    IFS=, read -r -a L <<< "${raw// /}"
    if [ "${#L[@]}" -ne 5 ]; then
        echo "M01_FAULT_LABELS: need five comma-separated labels, got: $raw" >&2; return 1
    fi
    for l in "${L[@]}"; do
        if ! [[ $l =~ ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,30}[a-z0-9]$ ]] \
           || [[ $l =~ ^(team|manual)[0-9]{2}$ ]] \
           || [[ " ns1 doq expired wrongds " == *" $l "* ]] \
           || [[ $seen == *" $l "* ]]; then
            echo "M01_FAULT_LABELS: bad, reserved or repeated label: $l" >&2; return 1
        fi
        seen+="$l "
    done
    M01_L_NOTSERVED=${L[0]} M01_L_DEAD=${L[1]} M01_L_GLUE=${L[2]} M01_L_NSSET=${L[3]} M01_L_NODELEG=${L[4]}
}
